## Don't edit this file; to overwrite any options, edit a file with a higher
## number that is read earlier by SSH, such as
## '/etc/ssh/ssh_config.d/10_user.conf'. If your configuration changes do not
## need to be system-wide, you may also consider placing overrides in
## ~/.ssh/config.

## See also:
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/SSH#Client_Configuration_File

Host *
  VisualHostKey yes
  ## Ciphers that are Terrapin-vulnerable when an outdated client or server are
  ## used are intentionally retained. Connecting to a Terrapin-vulnerable
  ## server cannot be made secure (as any Terrapin-vulnerable server will be
  ## vulnerable to other issues as well) and is therefore unsupported. Only
  ## ciphers providing AEAD are enabled by default.
  Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
  MACs umac-128-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com
  ## Only post-quantum-sequre KexAlgorithms are allowed.
  KexAlgorithms sntrup761x25519-sha512,sntrup761x25519-sha512@openssh.com,mlkem768x25519-sha256
  HostKeyAlgorithms sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com,ssh-ed25519
  PubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com,ssh-ed25519
